! Regression test: the scrolling pager must not spin when input runs out.
!
! print2()'s pager used to store getchar()'s result in a char, so it never
! recognized EOF: once the input was exhausted, metamath read EOF forever at
! 100% CPU, with its output half delivered.
!
! To reach the pager, this case turns prompted scrolling back on (the harness
! starts every case with SET SCROLL CONTINUOUS).  HEIGHT and HELP are chosen
! so that the displayed output does not fit on a single page, but are
! otherwise irrelevant.  The input ends right after HELP, while the pager is
! waiting for an answer, and metamath should stop that output and exit.
!
! The output is ignored, by the directive below: this case only checks that
! metamath terminates, so edits to the help text do not affect it.
!
! Caution: the harness applies no timeout, so a regression makes this case
! hang rather than fail.
!
! run_test
SET SCROLL PROMPTED
SET HEIGHT 1
HELP
